{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794426889,"nonce":"OOIGJJkV/cAzMTzjGpIXnGZMLG0=","message":"Correction to item 2 above: a library Step is one container, so the init container cannot come from lib:thulasi-ram/build. It comes from the placement profile: the profile adds an initContainer (aws ecr get-login-password into a shared emptyDir, medium Memory), the volume, a volumeMount and DOCKER_CONFIG on the step container, and the eks.amazonaws.com/skip-containers annotation for the step container. That needs d2b711b's strategic merge: with today's merge-patch, a profile's initContainers list would replace the egress sidecar and the workspace fetcher. Until d2b711b lands, the fallback is a narrow role with the identity in the build container (exposed to Dockerfile RUN, see df660b6).","files":null}]}